My framework is such that rallies from here until the end of the year are caused by 2 factors 

1. Lack of selling of stocks in general and best performers in particular to avoid taking capital gains in 2026.  Because so many investors with a diversified portfolio have LOTS of capital losses and modest capital gains this factor is DEAD

2. In years in which portfolio managers are doing very well in general there is pressure to pump the EOY to crystallize the maximum performance based compensation and if not performance based to at least retain AUM.  Furthermore underperformers tend to chase the strongest stocks so that by EOY they have caught up or at least have a portfolio that is more in line with the best performing funds.  As no one has strong performance and nothing to crystallize this factor is DEAD

